  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure B.1, first of three panels: alpha sweeps with 95% t-intervals for LCDB datasets 0-25 (T = 44, k = 22) — the appendix's full-corpus version of Figure 4.4. Nine datasets, normalised cumulative reward against α from 0.1 to 1.0. Most are close to flat between 0.84 and 0.94; ds 19 (pink) is the clear outlier, falling from 0.789 to 0.722 across the sweep and sitting about 0.09 below the next lowest. ds 25 leads at about 0.938 falling gently to 0.928; ds 12 and ds 16 rise slightly; ds 9 and ds 17 fall away after about α = 0.6.",
